  "customHelp": "DECK: exactly 50 cards, max 4 per card name. SETUP: Rock-paper-scissors; winner is first player (take the First Player token) and picks which side is Line 1. Draw 6, may mulligan once (whole hand). Put the top 5 cards of your deck face-down UPRIGHT into Hearts, and the top 1 card into Ena (unused = upright). ROUND = Summon Phase -> Battle Phase -> End Phase. SUMMON PHASE (first player, then second): Draw 1 (skip in round 1; if your deck is empty at Draw you LOSE). Ena Charge: may put 1 card from hand into Ena. Main: play Holobito by paying cost (tap that many Ena; at least one paid card - or the Overbeat base - must share each of the card's colors). New Line = your innermost empty line. Overbeat = stack on your own Holobito with LOWER cost, pay only the difference. Boost cannot be used in Summon Phase. BATTLE PHASE: resolve Line 1 to Line 5 (skip empty lines). On each line, starting with first player, alternate: use a Waza (put it sideways in that line), Boost (put a Boost Holobito sideways, pay its boost cost), or Pass. Both pass in a row -> compare power (Holobito + Waza/Boost on that line). Winner deals 1 damage to the opposing Holobito AND 1 damage to the opponent (Double Damage = 2). Tie: both Holobito take 1. Unopposed Holobito wins. DAMAGE: an upright card becomes DOWN (tap it); a card already down is DESTROYED. Player damage hits the top Heart. Destroyed Hearts go to Check Zone; after damage, for each: activate its Trigger (reveal it) or put it into your hand. Entry T: play it new-line or Overbeat free. Over T: Overbeat free. Draw T: discard it, draw 3. Last Over T: add to hand, draw 1; if you have 1 or fewer Hearts you may Overbeat it free. After each line, Waza/Boost cards there go to the graveyard. Whoever won Line 1 is first player next round (draw / no battle on Line 1 = swap). END PHASE: temporary power changes end. Slide: move Holobito inward to fill empty lines. Ena Draw: draw cards equal to your UNUSED (untapped) Ena. Then untap all Ena. LOSE: you take damage with no Hearts left, or you start your Draw step with an empty deck. EVENT TIEBREAK (time out, extra round still tied): most Hearts (down ones count), then most Holobito on field, then next round's first player wins.",
